   "text": "The drawing shows droxidopa, with a 3,4-dihydroxyphenyl ring on a CH(OH)\u2013CH(NH2)\u2013COOH chain.\n\n- **Ring:** a benzene ring with two adjacent OH groups (catechol) at the 3 and 4 positions relative to the chain attachment.\n- **Chain:** the ring carbon attaches to a CH carrying an OH on a wedge bond, then to a CH carrying an NH2 on a wedge bond, then to a carboxylic acid (C=O and OH).\n- **Stereocentre bearing OH:** the priorities are OH > CH(N) > aryl > H, with H pointing away. Going OH \u2192 CH(N) \u2192 aryl is clockwise, so this is R.\n- **Stereocentre bearing NH2:** the priorities are N > COOH > CH(OH) > H, with H pointing away. Going N \u2192 COOH \u2192 CH(OH) is counterclockwise, so this is S.\n\nThis gives (2S,3R)-2-amino-3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)-3-hydroxypropanoic acid. In the SMILES below, `@@` at the NH2 carbon encodes S and `@` at the OH carbon encodes R, which I checked by permuting the neighbour order.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H]([C@H](O)c1ccc(O)c(O)c1)C(=O)O"
